  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Indonesian Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka formally resigned from his office. The resignation process involved the submission of a five-paragraph letter to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), which officials have confirmed as the official notification marking the vacancy of the position. President Prabowo Subianto accepted the resignation with stated reluctance, acknowledging the career change and thanking the former vice president for his period of service. During the transition, members of the Gerindra party expressed their respect for the decision. The event has garnered significant public attention and was reported alongside concurrent economic news regarding the performance of the national currency. Legal experts and government ministers have confirmed the procedural validity of the document submitted, noting that the departure was initiated at the individual's own request.",
